---
import ProjectLayout from '../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import { Picture, Image } from 'astro:assets';
import studio from '../assets/jpl-studio.jpg';
import about from '../assets/jpl-about.png';
import inspoRoom from '../assets/inspo-room.png';
import inspoStudioSmall from '../assets/inspo-studiosmall.png';
import inspoMahdavi from '../assets/inspo-mahdavi.png';
import inspoAshby from '../assets/inspo-ashby.png';
---

<ProjectLayout title="Jesse Parris-Lamb Website Redesign (Unofficial) — rjrivera">
  <div class="project-header">
    <h1 class="project-title">Jesse Parris-Lamb Website Redesign (Unofficial)</h1>
    <div class="project-tags">
      <span>Web Design</span>
      <span>Front End</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="media-row">
    <div class="row-media project-hero-wrap">
      <Picture
        src={studio}
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        alt="Inside the Jesse Parris-Lamb studio — a walnut worktable with cane chairs against shelves of archive boxes and design books"
        widths={[768, 1280, 1600, 2000]}
        sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 880px"
        loading="eager"
        class="project-hero"
      />
      <div class="hero-scrim"></div>
      <div class="hero-marks">
        <img class="hero-wordmark" src="/jpl-wordmark.svg" alt="Jesse Parris-Lamb" />
        <img class="hero-monogram" src="/jpl-monogram-white.png" alt="" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row-text">
      <p>I recently moved to Brooklyn and have started to spend a few hours a day at The Brooklyn Public Library near Prospect Park to get some work done. I&rsquo;ve been looking for inspiration for my next project, and on my first day walking to the library in the morning, I walk past this interesting &ldquo;storefront&rdquo; that looked different from the rest on the street.</p>
      <p>I did a quick look on Apple Maps and saw it was the home of Jesse Parris-Lamb: a Brooklyn based interior design firm founded in 2014 &mdash; and they do really cool work. When I got to the library, I checked out their website and thought &ldquo;I can probably do better&rdquo; (humbly, of course) so here we are&hellip;</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="media-row">
    <div class="row-media">
      <p class="media-caption">The home page..</p>
      <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
        <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201950009?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row-text">
      <p>I wanted to try and capture the essence of JPL&rsquo;s design in this website. To me, they show a lot of expression, but a lot of restraint. They add a lot of character to spaces, a lot of flair&hellip; but it all seems very familiar and not overdone. That&rsquo;s tough to nail. So the website reflects the same principles: charming and familiar at face value, but very unique and intentional. Everything has to have a purpose.</p>
      <p>The goal of the home page was to get straight to the point. Get you into the world of Jesse Parris-Lamb as soon as you land on the website. I think the home page is a great execution of user guidance as well &mdash; tough to put into words, but I don&rsquo;t feel overwhelmed on the home page. I have everything I would want.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="media-row">
    <div class="row-media">
      <p class="media-caption">The interior gallery..</p>
      <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
        <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201950010?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row-text">
      <p>Interior gallery was an area I had to show a lot of restraint. Something bold or super &ldquo;experience&rdquo; heavy didn&rsquo;t fit into the vibe I had assigned to this project. A few nice touches went a long way here: a subtle parallax scroll and some hover effects to give the thumbnails some life.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="media-row">
    <div class="row-media">
      <p class="media-caption">A space gallery..</p>
      <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
        <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201950562?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row-text">
      <p>The gallery for each space was based off of reference image I generated for inspiration. I like how the large, off-center images sort of command a lot of space and attention, yet the write up to the left seems to have the same amount of pull. Idk, it was a fun use of spacing. The film strip on the bottom is a nice touch as well, the page felt incomplete and cheap without it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="media-row">
    <div class="row-media">
      <p class="media-caption">The about page..</p>
      <Picture
        src={about}
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        alt="The Jesse Parris-Lamb About page — a black-and-white monogram sculpture beside a portrait of the firm's founders"
        widths={[768, 1280, 1600, 2000]}
        sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 880px"
        loading="lazy"
        class="row-image"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="row-text">
      <p>Finally, the about page &mdash; which unironically is my favorite page of the project. I kept getting stuck trying to turn the about page into a whole experience, and it just never felt right. The original about page on JPL&rsquo;s site is very simple and plain, but that&rsquo;s why it&rsquo;s good. I came to the conclusion that the rest of the site is designed to be an experience for their work&hellip; the about page should not be competing with that. I want to see the story, and I want to see it quickly and all at once.</p>
      <p>I pulled inspiration from a website I had in my references that made really good use of full bleed images and color contrast. The other pages I had built were pretty uniform, so I felt that the about page was fair game for a slight departure in design. It feels special, but still not overdone.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="media-row">
    <div class="row-media">
      <p class="media-caption">The original site..</p>
      <div class="vimeo-wrapper">
        <iframe loading="lazy" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1201951169?autopause=0&muted=1&controls=0&loop=1&title=0&byline=0&portrait=0" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row-text">
      <p>Here is the original (current) website. It&rsquo;s fine, but it doesn&rsquo;t feel special. To me, it didn&rsquo;t reflect the level of work that Jesse Parris-Lamb does.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <p class="media-caption stack-caption">A few of my references..</p>
    <div class="stack-row">
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="stack-card stack-card-1">
          <Image src={inspoRoom} alt="Reference: a minimalist living room with a website on the screen" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="stack-card stack-card-2">
          <Image src={inspoStudioSmall} alt="Reference: StudioSmall website" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="stack-card stack-card-3">
          <Image src={inspoMahdavi} alt="Reference: India Mahdavi website" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="stack-card stack-card-4">
          <Image src={inspoAshby} alt="Reference: Studio Ashby website" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="460px" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="visit-block">
        <img class="visit-note" src="/click_to_visit_trim.png" alt="Click to visit the site" width="340" height="64" />
        <a class="omnibox" href="https://jpl-redesign.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the live JPL redesign at jpl-redesign.vercel.app">
          <svg class="omnibox-lock" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor"><path d="M11 7V5a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v2H4v7h8V7h-1zm-4-2a1 1 0 0 1 2 0v2H7V5z"/></svg>
          <span class="omnibox-url">jpl-redesign.vercel.app</span>
          <svg class="omnibox-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>

<script>
  // Each demo stays muted and plays only while in view, so we don't boot every
  // Vimeo player at once on load. Rebuilt on navigation; reuses players across visits.
  function initVimeoDemos() {
    const iframes = document.querySelectorAll('.vimeo-wrapper iframe');
    if (!iframes.length) return;

    const attach = () => {
      // @ts-ignore
      const reg = (window.__vimeoPlayers = window.__vimeoPlayers || new WeakMap());
      // @ts-ignore
      if (window.__vimeoObserver) window.__vimeoObserver.disconnect();

      const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach(entry => {
          const player = reg.get(entry.target);
          if (!player) return;
          if (entry.isIntersecting) {
            player.ready().then(() => player.setVolume(0)).then(() => player.play()).catch(() => {});
          } else {
            player.pause().then(() => player.setCurrentTime(0)).catch(() => {});
          }
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.5 });
      // @ts-ignore
      window.__vimeoObserver = observer;

      iframes.forEach(iframe => {
        let player = reg.get(iframe);
        if (!player) {
          // @ts-ignore
          player = new Vimeo.Player(iframe);
          player.setVolume(0);
          reg.set(iframe, player);
        }
        observer.observe(iframe);
      });
    };

    // @ts-ignore — reuse the API if it loaded on a previous visit.
    if (window.Vimeo && window.Vimeo.Player) {
      attach();
    } else {
      let api = document.getElementById('vimeo-api');
      if (!api) {
        api = document.createElement('script');
        api.id = 'vimeo-api';
        api.src = 'https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js';
        document.head.appendChild(api);
      }
      api.addEventListener('load', attach, { once: true });
    }
  }

  const runVimeoInit = () => requestAnimationFrame(() => initVimeoDemos());
  runVimeoInit();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', runVimeoInit);
  window.addEventListener('pageshow', (e) => { if (e.persisted) runVimeoInit(); });
</script>

<style>
  .project-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-family: Garamond, 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #1c1f23;
  }

  .project-tags {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .project-tags span {
    font-family: Garamond, 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #999;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Repeating row: media on the left, text on the right. */
  .media-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 1320px;
  }

  .media-row + .media-row {
    margin-top: 7rem;
  }

  .row-media {
    flex: 0 0 880px;
  }

  .row-text {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .row-text p {
    font-family: Garamond, 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #1c1f23;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .row-text p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .project-hero-wrap {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 2 / 1;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .media-caption {
    font-family: Garamond, 'EB Garamond', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #999;
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }

  .row-image {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .vimeo-wrapper {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 416 / 240;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .vimeo-wrapper iframe {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: none;
  }

  /* Closing "reference deck" — photos assemble into a jeu-de-paume-style pile. */
  .stack-section {
    margin-top: 9rem;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    max-width: 1320px;
  }

  .stack-caption {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    margin-left: 16px;
  }

  .stack-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3.5rem;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .stack {
    position: relative;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: clamp(300px, 40vw, 480px);
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
  }

  .visit-block {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 300px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: 13.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .visit-note {
    display: block;
    width: 340px;
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.8;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem 0.75rem;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .omnibox {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    background: #f1f3f4;
    border: 1px solid #e4e6e8;
    border-radius: 999px;
    text-decoration: none;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: background 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, transform 0.25s ease;
  }

  .omnibox:hover {
    background: #eceef0;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }

  .omnibox-lock {
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    color: #5f6368;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .omnibox-url {
    flex: 1;
    font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #202124;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

  .omnibox-arrow {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    color: #5f6368;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease, color 0.25s ease;
  }

  .omnibox:hover .omnibox-arrow {
    transform: translateX(4px);
    color: #202124;
  }

  /* Shimmer sweep on hover — feels like it's about to navigate */
  .omnibox::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: -60%;
    width: 55%;
    height: 100%;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75), transparent);
    transform: skewX(-20deg);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .omnibox:hover::after {
    animation: omnibox-shimmer 0.9s ease;
  }

  @keyframes omnibox-shimmer {
    from { left: -60%; }
    to { left: 130%; }
  }

  .stack-card {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.20);
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }

  .stack-card :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Resting positions (also the static fallback when motion is reduced). */
  .stack-card-1 { z-index: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(-16px, 14px) rotate(-7deg); }
  .stack-card-2 { z-index: 2; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(12px, 8px) rotate(5deg); }
  .stack-card-3 { z-index: 3; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(-6px, 0) rotate(-3deg); }
  .stack-card-4 { z-index: 4; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) translate(8px, -8px) rotate(2deg); }

  /* Card 1 is the base of the pile — it's always present and never animates. */
  .stack-card-2 { animation: stack2 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
  .stack-card-3 { animation: stack3 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }
  .stack-card-4 { animation: stack4 2.6s linear infinite alternate; }

  @keyframes stack2 {
    0%, 8%   { opacity: 0; }
    9%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  }
  @keyframes stack3 {
    0%, 38%  { opacity: 0; }
    39%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  }
  @keyframes stack4 {
    0%, 68%  { opacity: 0; }
    69%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .stack-card { animation: none; opacity: 1; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .media-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .row-media {
      flex: none;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .stack-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  .project-hero {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 72%;
    display: block;
  }

  .hero-scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,0.12), rgba(0,0,0,0.34));
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hero-marks {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hero-monogram {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    width: min(72%, 384px);
    height: auto;
  }

  .hero-wordmark {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    bottom: 1.4rem;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: min(22%, 120px);
    height: auto;
    filter: brightness(0) invert(1) drop-shadow(0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.35));
  }
</style>
